TEXT -312 -64 Left 5 ;NOTE: The simulation waveform output time starts at 500ms (500ms = time zero)
TEXT -296 440 Left 5 ;In this example there are 2x 400MW Generators present.\nThe loadsteps are at 4s, 6s and 11s with each 100MW\nLoadstep 1 and 2 are taken mainly by gen1, Loadstep 3 is taken mainly by\ngen2. At t=15s till t=18s the Transformer taping is set from 0 to 15 for transformer1\nand 0 till -15 for transformer2. Since the taping is for the phase shift the\nactive power flow is changing. You can see that now Gen1 is unburdened a lot\nand gen2 is more burdened.   \nStator voltage of gen2 is controlled  \nby AVR whereas the voltage level of gen1 is set manually.
